START  open the app  FIND A PLACE TO SHOW    if the person has a selected saved location:      viewingPlace = that location    else:      viewingPlace = none      show "Search for a city or use your location"  GET THE WEATHER for viewingPlace    if a saved forecast is younger than 30 minutes: use it    else if the internet is on: ask Open-Meteo, save a copy on the device    else: use the last saved copy and show "You are offline"  SHOW THE WEATHER    current weather: temperature, humidity, wind speed, feels like, rain chance    the Hourly / Daily choice (Hourly first)    the forecast for the choice    check for severe weather: show a banner and send a notification  WHILE the app is open:    wait for the person to do something    if they search for a city        -> show matching places, view the one they pick    if they click "Use my location"  -> explain, ask permission, view their weather    if they click "Save location"    -> save the place being viewed    if they pick a saved location    -> view its weather    if they switch Hourly / Daily    -> change the forecast shown    if they change a setting         -> apply and save it (a new unit gets the weather again)    if the internet drops            -> show the saved weather with an offline banner    if the internet returns          -> get fresh weather by itself  END WHILEENDROUTESSTART  function App():    wrap everything in SettingsProvider    wrap everything in LocationsProvider    wrap everything in ToastProvider    show Navbar on every page    routes:      "/"          -> Weather      "/locations" -> Locations      "/settings"  -> Settings      anything else -> NotFoundENDWEATHER PAGESTART  function Weather():    state: viewingPlace = selected saved location, or none    state: forecast = none, isLoading = false, lastUpdated = none    state: isOffline = not navigator.onLine    state: view = "hourly", errorMessage = ""  WHEN THE PAGE LOADS:    if viewingPlace is none:      show the empty state: "Search for a city or use your location"    else:      loadForecast(viewingPlace)  WHEN viewingPlace OR the units in settings CHANGE:    loadForecast(viewingPlace)  WHEN THE BROWSER GOES ONLINE:    isOffline = false    loadForecast(viewingPlace)               (refresh by itself)  WHEN THE BROWSER GOES OFFLINE:    isOffline = true  function loadForecast(place):    isLoading = true    errorMessage = ""    cached = storageGet(cacheKey(place), none)    if cached exists and cached is younger than 30 minutes and cached.units equals unitsInSettings():      forecast = cached.data      lastUpdated = cached.savedAt      isLoading = false      return                                  (no server call needed, so it loads fast)    if the browser is online:      try:        data = getForecast(place.latitude, place.longitude, settings)        forecast = data        lastUpdated = now        storageSet(cacheKey(place), { savedAt: now, units: unitsInSettings(), data })        checkAlerts(data, place)      catch:        useCacheOrShowError(cached)    else:      useCacheOrShowError(cached)    isLoading = false  function useCacheOrShowError(cached):    if cached exists:      forecast = cached.data      lastUpdated = cached.savedAt      showToast("error", "Could not update. Showing saved weather.")    else:      errorMessage = "No saved weather for this place yet. Connect to the internet and try again."      show a "Try again" button -> loadForecast(viewingPlace)  function onSaveLocationClick():    if viewingPlace is already saved:      showToast("error", viewingPlace.name + " is already saved")    else:      addLocation(viewingPlace)  function onSavedChipClick(location):    selectLocation(location.id)    viewingPlace = location  function onViewChanged(newView):    view = newView                            ("hourly" or "daily")ENDSHOWING THE WEATHERSTART  function display():    show search box, "Use my location" button, "Save location" button    show a chip for each saved location (the one being viewed is highlighted)    if isOffline:      show banner "You are offline. Showing weather saved at " + formatTime(lastUpdated)    if isLoading: show loader    else if errorMessage is not empty: show errorMessage and the "Try again" button    else if forecast exists:      show currentWeatherCard()      show alert banner for each active alert      show the Hourly / Daily toggle      if view == "hourly": show hourlyForecast()      else: show dailyForecast()  function currentWeatherCard():    show place name and "Updated " + formatTime(lastUpdated)    show icon and description from describeWeather(forecast.current.weatherCode)    show temperature with the unit (C or F)    show humidity as a percentage    show wind speed with the unit (km/h or mph)    show feels like and rain chance  function hourlyForecast():    now = forecast.current.time            (the place's own local time, not the browser's)    hours = the next HOURS_SHOWN hours, starting from the hour that contains now    for each hour in hours:      show time (24-hour or 12-hour, from settings)      show icon, temperature, and rain chance  function dailyForecast():    days = the next DAYS_SHOWN days    for each day in days:      show day name ("Today", then weekday names)      show icon, lowest and highest temperature, and rain chance  function describeWeather(code):    0           -> "Clear", sun icon    1, 2, 3     -> "Partly cloudy", cloud icon    45, 48      -> "Fog"    51 to 67    -> "Rain or drizzle", rain icon    71 to 77    -> "Snow"    80 to 82    -> "Showers", rain icon    95 to 99    -> "Thunderstorm"    anything else -> "Unknown"ENDUSING THE PERSON'S LOCATIONSTART  function onUseMyLocationClick():    show the explanation popup    (it says why location is needed, that your rounded position is kept on this device and sent to the     weather service, Open-Meteo, to get the forecast, and that the browser will ask next)  function onNotNowClick():    close the popup  function onAllowClick():    if the browser has no location support:      show "Location is not available. Search for a city instead."      focus the search box      return    isLocating = true    ask the browser for the position (wait at most LOCATION_TIMEOUT)    on success:      latitude  = round(position.latitude, 2)       (about 1 km, for privacy)      longitude = round(position.longitude, 2)      place = { name: "My location", latitude, longitude, isCurrent: true }      remove any older location where isCurrent is true      addLocation(place)      close the popup      showToast("success", "Showing weather for your location")    on error:      if the person blocked it:        show "Location is off. Search for a city, or turn it on in your browser settings."      else if it timed out or is unavailable:        show "We could not find your location. Try again or search for a city."      focus the search box    finally:      isLocating = falseENDSEARCHING FOR A CITYSTART  state: text = "", results = [], isSearching = false, searchError = ""  function onSearchTyped(newText):    text = newText    cancel any search that is still waiting    if text.length < SEARCH_MIN_LENGTH:      results = []      return    wait SEARCH_DELAY, then runSearch(text)       (so we do not call the server on every key)  function runSearch(text):    isSearching = true    searchError = ""    try:      results = searchPlaces(text)    catch:      if the browser is offline:        searchError = "You are offline. Saved places still work."      else:        searchError = "Search failed. Please try again."      results = []    finally:      isSearching = false  function display():    search box    if isSearching: show loader    else if searchError is not empty: show searchError    else if text is long enough and results is empty: show "No places match " + text    else for each place in results:      show: name, region, country      if place is already saved: show "Already saved" and do not allow a click      else: clicking it -> onResultClick(place)  function onResultClick(place):    viewingPlace = place            (viewed, not saved yet)    clear text and resultsENDWEATHER ALERTSSTART  function checkAlerts(data, place):    found = []    look at the next 24 hours of data and compare with ALERT RULES    (the temperature limits are in degrees C, so convert the forecast to C first if the person uses F)    for each rule that matches, add { id, type, message } to found      id = cacheKey(place) + type + the place's date      (one alert per kind per day)    activeAlerts = found                            (these show in the banner)    if settings.alertsOn is false: return    shown = storageGet("weather.alertsShown", [])    for each alert in found:      if alert.id is in shown: skip      sendNotification(alert, place)      shown.add(alert.id)    remove entries from earlier days, so the list does not grow forever    storageSet("weather.alertsShown", shown)  function sendNotification(alert, place):    (browser notifications only appear while the app is open in a tab)    if the browser does not support notifications: return    if Notification.permission == "granted":      show notification: title = "Weather alert: " + place.name, body = alert.message  function onAlertsSwitchChanged(on):    if on is true:      if Notification.permission == "default":        result = ask the browser for permission        if result != "granted":          updateSetting("alertsOn", false)          showToast("error", "Notifications are blocked. Turn them on in your browser settings.")          return      if Notification.permission == "denied":        updateSetting("alertsOn", false)        showToast("error", "Notifications are blocked. Turn them on in your browser settings.")        return    updateSetting("alertsOn", on)ENDLOCATIONS PAGESTART  function Locations():    state: addOpen = false  function display():    show "Saved locations" and the number of places    show "+ Add a location" button -> addOpen = true    if locations is empty:      show "No saved places yet" and a button to the Weather page    else for each location in locations:      cached = storageGet(cacheKey(location), none)      show card:        name, country        "My location" tag if isCurrent        temperature and condition from cached, or "No saved weather" if none        if location.id == selectedId: show "Viewing now"        else: show "View weather" button -> onViewClick(location)        Remove button -> removeLocation(location.id)    show "Your saved places are stored on this device only" and a "Clear my data" link    if addOpen: show AddLocationPopup  function onViewClick(location):    selectLocation(location.id)    goTo("/")  function AddLocationPopup():    uses the same search steps as SEARCHING FOR A CITY    clicking a result:      addLocation(place)           (saves it and shows the green message)      addOpen = false    Escape, Cancel or clicking outside:      addOpen = false, focus returns to the "+ Add a location" buttonENDSETTINGS PAGESTART  function Settings():    show Theme: three choices (light, dark, lime)      clicking one -> updateSetting("theme", choice)    show Units:      temperature: C or F   -> updateSetting("temperatureUnit", choice)      wind speed: km/h or mph -> updateSetting("windUnit", choice)      time: 24-hour or 12-hour -> updateSetting("timeFormat", choice)    show Alerts switch -> onAlertsSwitchChanged(on)    show "Clear my data" button -> onClearClick()  function onClearClick():    ask "Clear all saved places and settings?"    if the person confirms: clearAllData()  A unit change makes the Weather page ask for the forecast again in the new units.ENDNOT FOUNDSTART  function NotFound():    show "404" and "This page does not exist"    show "Back to weather" button -> goTo("/")ENDDATA (localStorage)START  KEYS    "weather.locations"      = [ { id, name, region, country, latitude, longitude, isCurrent } ]    "weather.selectedId"     = id of the location being viewed, or none    "weather.settings"       = { theme, temperatureUnit, windUnit, timeFormat, alertsOn }    "weather.cache.{latitude},{longitude}" = { savedAt, units, data }                             one saved forecast per place, keyed by rounded coordinates,                             so it also works for a place that is not saved yet    "weather.alertsShown"    = [ alertId ]           alerts already shown, so none repeat  DEFAULT_SETTINGS = { theme: "light", temperatureUnit: "C", windUnit: "kmh", timeFormat: "24h", alertsOn: false }ENDCONSTANTSSTART  THEMES            = ["light", "dark", "lime"]  TEMPERATURE_UNITS = ["C", "F"]  WIND_UNITS        = ["kmh", "mph"]  TIME_FORMATS      = ["24h", "12h"]  VIEWS             = ["hourly", "daily"]  SEARCH_MIN_LENGTH = 2 letters  SEARCH_DELAY      = 400 milliseconds  LOCATION_TIMEOUT  = 10 seconds  HOURS_SHOWN       = next 24 hours  DAYS_SHOWN        = 7 days  TOAST_TIME        = 3 seconds  ALERT RULES (checked against the next 24 hours)    thunderstorm  : weather code is 95, 96 or 99    strong wind   : wind gusts of 60 km/h or more    heavy rain    : 10 mm or more of rain expected within 6 hours    extreme heat  : 35 degrees C or more    freezing cold : 0 degrees C or lessENDSTORAGE HELPERSSTART  function storageGet(key, fallback):    try:      text = localStorage.getItem(key)      if text is none: return fallback      return parse(text)    catch:      return fallback            (broken or blocked storage never crashes the app)  function storageSet(key, value):    try: localStorage.setItem(key, text(value))    catch: showToast("error", "Could not save on this device")  function storageRemove(key):    try: localStorage.removeItem(key)  function cacheKey(place):    return "weather.cache." + round(place.latitude, 2) + "," + round(place.longitude, 2)  function unitsInSettings():    return { temperature: settings.temperatureUnit, wind: settings.windUnit }ENDSERVER CALLS (Open-Meteo, no API key needed)START  function searchPlaces(text):    return GET geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search?name={text}&count=8    return only the list of results, or an empty list if there are none  function getForecast(latitude, longitude, settings):    return GET api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast with      latitude, longitude, timezone = auto      current = temperature, humidity, feels like, weather code, wind speed, rain      hourly  = temperature, rain chance, rain amount, wind gusts, weather code      daily   = weather code, highest temp, lowest temp, rain chance      temperature_unit = "celsius" if settings.temperatureUnit is "C", otherwise "fahrenheit"      wind_speed_unit  = settings.windUnit            ("kmh" or "mph")  if a call fails with an error status: throw an error so the caller can show a messageENDSETTINGS CONTEXTSTART  function SettingsProvider():    settings = storageGet("weather.settings", DEFAULT_SETTINGS)    WHEN settings.theme CHANGES:      set the page's data-theme to settings.theme      (colours change through CSS variables)    function updateSetting(name, value):      settings[name] = value      storageSet("weather.settings", settings)    function clearAllData():      remove every key that starts with "weather."      settings = DEFAULT_SETTINGS      locations = []      selectedId = none      showToast("success", "Your data was cleared")    share settings, updateSetting, clearAllData with every pageENDLOCATIONS CONTEXTSTART  function LocationsProvider():    locations  = storageGet("weather.locations", [])    selectedId = storageGet("weather.selectedId", none)    function addLocation(place):      if a saved location has the same rounded latitude and longitude:        showToast("error", place.name + " is already saved")        return      place.id = newId()      locations.add(place)      selectedId = place.id      save locations and selectedId      showToast("success", place.name + " saved to your locations")    function removeLocation(id):      removed = the location with this id      locations.remove(id)      storageRemove(cacheKey(removed))      if selectedId == id:        selectedId = first saved location, or none      save locations and selectedId      showToast("success", "Location removed")    function selectLocation(id):      selectedId = id      save selectedId    share locations, selectedId, addLocation, removeLocation, selectLocationENDTOASTSSTART  function ToastProvider():    state: messages = []  function showToast(type, message):    item = { id: newId(), type, message }    messages.add(item)    after TOAST_TIME: messages.remove(item)  display:    for each item in messages:      show a pop-up in its colour (success = green, error = red)      announce it to screen readersENDPERFORMANCESTART  load each page only when it is opened (lazy loading)  wait SEARCH_DELAY before searching, and cancel a search that is no longer needed  use the saved forecast if it is younger than 30 minutes  only recalculate the hourly and daily lists when the forecast or units change  show a loader while waiting, so the page never looks frozenENDPRIVACY AND SECURITYSTART  ask for location only after the person clicks "Allow location", and explain why first  round coordinates to 2 decimal places before saving them  store everything on the device only; no account, no tracking, no cookies  the only thing sent out is the rounded position, to Open-Meteo, to get the forecast; say so in the popup and the README  the weather service needs no key, so there is no secret in the code  show text from the server only as plain text (React escapes it)  "Clear my data" removes every "weather." keyENDRESPONSIVE AND ACCESSIBLESTART  breakpoints: 320, 480, 768, 1024, 1200    320 and 480: one column, hourly cards scroll sideways, chips wrap, buttons full width    768:         the stats sit under the temperature, saved locations show two per row    1024 and up: current card in two columns, saved locations show three per row  every input has a label; popups close with Escape and keep focus inside  alerts and messages are announced to screen readers  weather is shown with text as well as icons and colourEND
